# Directory Structure — NestJS

## Standard structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                     ← Bootstrap: NestFactory.create()
├── app.module.ts               ← Root module
└── modules/
    └── <domain>/               ← One directory per domain (users, auth, products)
        ├── <domain>.module.ts  ← Module: imports, providers, exports
        ├── <domain>.controller.ts ← Routes, request/response handling only
        ├── <domain>.service.ts ← Business logic
        ├── dto/
        │   ├── create-<domain>.dto.ts
        │   └── update-<domain>.dto.ts
        ├── entities/
        │   └── <domain>.entity.ts
        └── <domain>.spec.ts    ← Unit tests

common/
├── filters/                    ← Global exception filters
├── guards/                     ← Auth guards
├── interceptors/               ← Logging, transform response
├── decorators/                 ← Custom decorators
└── pipes/                      ← Custom validation pipes
```

## Principles

- **Controller** handles HTTP only — calls service, returns response. No business logic.
- **Service** contains all business logic. No dependency on `Request`/`Response`.
- **DTO** validates all incoming data using `class-validator`
- **Module** encapsulates its domain — expose only what other modules need via `exports`
